+# Q03 P0: full-import registration and fake-dispatch smoke
+
+Purpose: replace the earlier AST-only/string-only registration evidence with
+actual serving-module imports and real operator registrations in two isolated
+processes. This is not a real MoE execution test or a substitute for opcheck,
+functionalization, CUDA graphs, numerical or performance gates.
+
+## Safety and scope
+
+`--list` and Python syntax checks use only the standard library. `--run` imports
+Torch, the full MoE runner/backend and the DeepSeek V4.1 NVIDIA model module.
+Those imports may load native libraries, discover devices or initialize CUDA.
+Do not call this CPU-only merely because its operator inputs are FakeTensors.
+Run only in an independently approved isolated environment. The acknowledgment
+flag records operator intent, not permission to use a device or service.
+No model instance, weights, real tensor allocation, real MoE call or cluster
+operation is requested by the test itself. Dependency imports remain observable
+platform work. No packages are installed or platform registrations replaced.
+
+## Commands
+
+From the new, clean, committed candidate vLLM checkout, using the approved
+existing environment's Python (shown as `.venv/bin/python`):
+
+```sh
+.venv/bin/python tests/standalone_tests/deepseek_v41_q03_registration.py --list
+.venv/bin/python -m py_compile tests/standalone_tests/deepseek_v41_q03_registration.py
+```
+
+Only after approval for the selected environment and its import/device effects:
+
+```sh
+.venv/bin/python tests/standalone_tests/deepseek_v41_q03_registration.py \
+  --run --allow-platform-initialization --expected-platform cuda \
+  --expected-head FULL_NEW_CANDIDATE_COMMIT \
+  --runtime-manifest /APPROVED_RESULTS/reviewed-candidate-runtime.json \
+  --output-dir /APPROVED_RESULTS/p0-registration-run-01
+```
+
+Use a fresh output directory for every attempt; preserve failed logs. A genuinely
+approved CPU environment can name `--expected-platform cpu`, but that result
+must be labeled CPU-platform evidence, not target-CUDA registration evidence.
+Do not force vLLM's platform to CUDA or use dependency stubs to obtain a pass.
+
+## What each process verifies
+
+- `default`: removes only the inherited `VLLM_USE_LAYERNAME` override, records
+  that inherited value, and uses actual package defaults. Opaque LayerName must
+  actually be supported and enabled; otherwise the run is unexecuted/nonzero.
+- `string`: explicitly sets `VLLM_USE_LAYERNAME=0` before any serving import.
+- Normal imports must resolve to the reviewed installation root. Both wheel
+  and reviewed editable candidate installations are accepted, including one
+  rooted in the prepared checkout. No sys.path overlay is injected. The nine
+  relevant source files must match this expected checkout byte for byte;
+  imported Python modules must share the reviewed package root, and each native
+  extension must match its independently recorded build origin and hash.
+  Imported hashes, Torch/CUDA-build version, actual platform/dispatch key,
+  LayerName mode and CUDA initialization state are saved.
+- The reviewed runtime manifest must bind the candidate HEAD to exact package
+  versions, installation mode/root and both native vLLM extension origins/hashes. Produce it from independently
+  verified candidate build/install receipts, not from an unchecked runtime just
+  to satisfy the test. A baseline image with candidate Python mounted over it
+  is not evidence of a complete candidate installation.
+- Both bridge operators retain explicit read-only q/sf and their expected
+  mutation schemas. Calls go through actual `torch.ops` and FakeTensor dispatch,
+  not a direct fake function. Both output arities, shape/dtype/device, no output
+  input alias, malformed scale dtype/width, rows0/1/6/16/96/8192 and optional
+  shared-input metadata are checked.
+
+Both processes and complete reports must pass; missing dependencies, missing
+reports, wrong mode, timeout or assertion failure cannot be skipped into green.
+Exit 0 means this bounded smoke passed, not all P0/compiler/runtime gates.
+Native logs and mode JSON reports accompany summary.json. The current test
+contains no `torch.library.opcheck`, AOT functionalization or real operator
+execution; those remain separate, explicitly unexecuted gates.
+
+## Required reviewed runtime manifest
+
+The exact source HEAD is the new committed test candidate used above. The target
+versions supplied for this work are Python 3.12.3, Torch 2.13.0+cu130, TileLang
+0.1.15 and TileKernels 2.0.0, not the earlier local Torch 2.14.1 probe environment.
+The two native hashes must come from the approved candidate build evidence;
+placeholders are deliberately not runnable values:
+
+```json
+{
+  "source_head": "FULL_NEW_CANDIDATE_COMMIT",
+  "installation": {
+    "mode": "wheel",
+    "package_root": "/APPROVED_INSTALL/vllm"
+  },
+  "versions": {
+    "python": "3.12.3",
+    "torch": "2.13.0+cu130",
+    "tilelang": "0.1.15",
+    "tile_kernels": "2.0.0"
+  },
+  "native_paths": {
+    "vllm._C_stable_libtorch": "/APPROVED_BUILD/_C_stable_libtorch.so",
+    "vllm._moe_C_stable_libtorch": "/APPROVED_BUILD/_moe_C_stable_libtorch.so"
+  },
+  "native_sha256": {
+    "vllm._C_stable_libtorch": "REVIEWED_SHA256",
+    "vllm._moe_C_stable_libtorch": "REVIEWED_SHA256"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Until that installation and manifest exist, full-candidate P0 is unexecuted.
+An approved different environment must have its own reviewed manifest and
+clearly labeled evidence; do not silently substitute package versions.
+
+For an approved editable installation set mode to `editable` and record its
+actual package root and native build paths. A verified editable build is not
+rejected merely for residing in the prepared checkout; unknown/unverified
+origins or an unrecorded Python overlay remain errors.
